# M31 fixture tm_tso_ordering — subscriber golden (SKELETON, ORDER-CRITICAL).
# expected.subscriber.log
# attestation: spec-derived from IEEE 1516.1-2010 references below
# Cross-check status: NOT CROSS-CHECKED — fixture uses >2 federates; exceeds the free-edition federate cap of the reference RTI used for local cross-checks. Independently verifiable against any DLC-conformant RTI via the PRTI_HOME-gated harness. See docs/PITCH_PARITY.md.
# canonicalization: cppsdk/tests/dlc/conformance/_harness/normalize.py
# spec-cites: see README.md
#
# CRITICAL: lines 5..7 below are in spec-canonical TSO tie-break order.
# Per §5.2.1 of docs/DLC_COMPLIANCE_PROGRAM.md, log_diff MUST NOT sort
# within an LBTS bucket for TSO. RO would be allowed to sort; TSO is not.
#
# Per §8.15 the spec mandates: within a single logical-time bucket, TSO
# deliveries are ordered by ascending FederateHandle. Publishers join in
# the canonical order [alice, bob, carol] so their handles are ascending.
#
# M38 GA re-derivation: the subscriber NER-walks to t=2 via repeated
# nextMessageRequest(2.0). §8.8: with the publishers' T=1.0 Ticks queued
# while the first NMR is pending, that request COMPLETES at
# min(2.0, 1.0) = 1.0 — GRANT 1.0 lands after the three RECVs (§8.14);
# the re-issued NMR(2.0) then grants at 2.0 once the publishers'
# advance/resign lifts LBTS past it. The pre-M38 golden modelled a
# single GRANT 2.0 (the "no pending message" timeline), which is
# unreachable here: the fixture's launch protocol guarantees the NMR is
# issued (GALT-gated) before the dwell-delayed T=1.0 sends.
SUB: CONNECT                                                           # §4.2
SUB: JOIN federate=sub                                                 # §4.9
SUB: SUBSCRIBE interaction=Tick active=true                            # §5.6 (catalogue 11.11 — active flag)
SUB: TIME_CONSTRAINED_ENABLED time=0.000000                            # §8.6
SUB: RECV interaction=Tick time=1.000000 seq=1 source=alice order=TIMESTAMP  # §8.15 — lowest FederateHandle wins tie-break
SUB: RECV interaction=Tick time=1.000000 seq=1 source=bob order=TIMESTAMP    # §8.15
SUB: RECV interaction=Tick time=1.000000 seq=1 source=carol order=TIMESTAMP  # §8.15
SUB: GRANT time=1.000000                                               # §8.8 — NMR(2.0) completes at min(2.0, next-TSO-time 1.0), AFTER the deliveries (§8.14)
SUB: GRANT time=2.000000                                               # §8.13 — re-issued NMR(2.0); no TSO left, grant at the requested time
SUB: RESIGN action=CANCEL_THEN_DELETE_THEN_DIVEST                      # §4.10
